    "narrative": "The primary engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads our lineup with a 75.69 efficiency score. His matchup against Kevin Gausman is mitigated by the 86% stolen base probability against a pitcher with a traditionally slow delivery, making him our highest-priority asset in the pursuit of the scarce SB category. **Seiya Suzuki** also projects as a strong start (71.14), benefiting from a favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly (xERA 5.27). While **Henry Bolte** (61.01) is boosted by his leadoff spot and a decent matchup against Zebby Matthews, the rest of our core\u2014including **Max Muncy** (59.65) and **Mickey Moniak** (57.78)\u2014sits in the middle-ground, requiring careful monitoring of official lineups to ensure they remain in high-leverage spots.\n\nWe are navigating a tough day against some elite arms; specifically, **Josh Naylor** (47.41) faces a formidable test against Zack Wheeler. While **Naylor** is a staple, his score is suppressed by the -19% SP skill penalty, leaving him on the borderline of our bench threshold. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Griffin Conine**, whose 35.44 score fell just short of the active roster. While **Conine** possesses an impressive xwOBA, the combination of a negative platoon disadvantage against Ranger Suarez and an unfavorable batting order position made him the first man out. We continue to manage injury risks elsewhere, with **Tyler Soderstrom** remaining on the IL and **Vinnie Pasquantino** unavailable due to the team\u2019s off-day. \n\nFinally, managers should be on high alert regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across our roster, particularly for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Travis Bazzana**. If **Moreno** drops from the #3 spot in the batting order, his 56.63 score will likely crater, potentially forcing a defensive sub to protect our daily cap. We are also keeping a close eye on **Zach McKinstry**; while he is currently active, his low score of 40.98 makes him the most volatile asset in our lineup, and any negative shifts in wind direction or lineup placement will likely lead to an immediate benching to preserve our limited game volume.",
